1. Scope and definitions

This license applies to the original code, documentation, and artwork in this
release of DND Card Web, except material identified as having another license
(the "Software"). "You" includes a person or organization exercising rights
under this license. "Licensor" means the copyright holders of the Software.

A "Covered Work" is the Software or a work that modifies, adapts, incorporates,
or is otherwise derived from a substantial copyright-protected portion of it.
A separate, independent program is not a Covered Work merely because it is
stored alongside the Software, communicates through an ordinary interface,
or was used to produce or run it.

"Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for commercial advantage or
monetary compensation, including selling or licensing a Covered Work,
charging for access, subscriptions, hosting or related paid functionality,
advertising or sponsorship monetization, or using it to provide paid services.
A charge described as covering hosting costs is still a charge for access.
Unconditional voluntary donations are not Commercial Use if they confer no
access, features, priority, services, or other consideration and the activity
is not otherwise primarily intended for commercial advantage. Mere use by an
individual employed by a business does not itself make personal recreational
use commercial.

"Corresponding Source" is the complete preferred form for making changes to
a Covered Work, including all modifications, incorporated covered modules,
interface definitions, build and installation scripts, dependency manifests,
and configuration templates needed to build, install, and run that version.
Obfuscated or minified code alone is not Corresponding Source. Independent
standard tools or dependencies available separately under their own licenses
may be identified by exact version and accessible source location. Secrets,
credentials, user records, private character data, and independent third-party
rule databases are not required; use documented placeholders and data-loading
interfaces instead. Material must not be withheld merely by moving covered
code into another repository or service.

