3. Distribution, network services, and source availability

If You distribute a Covered Work in any form, or make it available for use by
other people over a network, You must:

(a) Publish the complete Corresponding Source of the exact version offered,
    under this same license, at a publicly accessible network location,
    without a fee, subscription, or mandatory account.
(b) Provide a clear, readily accessible source link and license link with
    distributed copies and in the user interface of any network service.
    The source must be downloadable, not merely viewable through a service.
(c) Keep that source available for as long as the network service is offered
    and for at least three years after Your last distribution of that version
    or Your last provision of that version as a network service, whichever
    occurs later. A public source repository with downloadable revisions is
    sufficient while it meets these requirements.
(d) Include this license, retain copyright and attribution notices, identify
    material modifications and their authors, and avoid implying endorsement
    by the original project or any other contributor.

These requirements apply to original and modified versions, including
self-hosted services made available to other people. A publicly distributed
Covered Work as a whole must remain under this license. You may not use a
more permissive license, impose further restrictions on the rights granted
here, or use technical measures that prevent recipients from exercising them.
Independent dependencies remain subject to their own licenses; if their terms
cannot be satisfied together with this license, You have no permission under
this license to distribute the incompatible combination.

